(Nested-list edge cases - plan 040 stage 1e1. An empty nested list
 renders []; a nested list as the first element classifies correctly;
 a list-of-lists literal iterated directly yields list-typed loop vars;
 and `is a list` folds to true on a statically-typed list variable.)

a list called withempty is [1, [], 2].
print withempty.
a list called lead is [[1, 2], 3].
print lead.
print element 1 of lead.
for each row in [[10, 20], [30, 40]], print row.
a list called static is [1, 2, 3].
if static is a list
  print "yes"
otherwise
  print "no"